    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, the audit rights part is crucial. I'm just really concerned about those small, unpredictable things that can go wrong—those little \"glitches\" in the process where someone might intentionally manipulate small numbers or cause minor disruptions to gain an advantage. Is there a way to include provisions for \"small-scale\" misconduct or subtle bad faith, rather than just major breaches?",
